-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: what an amendment, a repeal and a repeal with
-- replacement do and do not imply (ss 34, 36(1)(b), 36(1)(c) and 37). The rest of s 35 and s 36 is in
-- `bc-interpretation-repeal.l4`, which this file imports for its refusal where no enactment is substituted.
--
-- What FALSE and REFUSE mean here (NOTES.md, finding 2). TRUE: the case is within the provision and the provision gives the
-- thing. FALSE: only where the words of the provision give the negative themselves (an exception, "is not", "must ... one
-- whose"). REFUSE: the case is outside what the provision speaks of, or the provision only permits or "includes" and the
-- case is not listed; the text is silent and a default would be a guess.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-repeal`

§ `s 34 Amending enactment part of the enactment amended`

-- src:383 | 34 An amending enactment must be construed as part of the enactment that it amends.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 34 (src:383)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34 speaks only of an amending enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 34 speaks only of an amending enactment"

-- src:383 | 34 An amending enactment must be construed as part of the enactment that it amends.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 34 (src:383)
GIVEN `the enactment is an amending enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34 the enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends` `the enactment is an amending enactment` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment is an amending enactment`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 34 speaks only of an amending enactment`

§ `s 36(1)(b) and (c) Proceedings after repeal and replacement`

-- src:397 | (b) every proceeding commenced under the former enactment must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(b) (src:397)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(b) speaks only of a proceeding commenced under the former enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 36(1)(b) speaks only of a proceeding commenced under the former enactment"

-- "so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment" is a limit in the words, so a proceeding that cannot be
-- continued consistently gets FALSE.
-- src:395 | 36 (1) If an enactment (the "former enactment") is repealed and another enactment (the "new enactment") is substituted for it,
-- src:397 | (b) every proceeding commenced under the former enactment must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment so far as it may be done consistently with the new enactment,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(b) (src:395, src:397)
GIVEN `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding was commenced under the former enactment`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuing it under the new enactment is consistent with the new enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(b) the proceeding must be continued under and in conformity with the new enactment` `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment` `the proceeding was commenced under the former enactment` `continuing it under the new enactment is consistent with the new enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment` THEN `s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one`
        IF NOT `the proceeding was commenced under the former enactment` THEN `s 36(1)(b) speaks only of a proceeding commenced under the former enactment`
        OTHERWISE `continuing it under the new enactment is consistent with the new enactment`

DECLARE `Where the procedure of the new enactment is followed` IS ONE OF
    `The recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment`
    `The enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment`
    `A proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal`
    `Something else`

-- src:398 | (c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed as far as it can be adapted in the recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment, in the enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment, and in a proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(c) (src:398)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(c) names three situations in which the procedure of the new enactment is followed and no others` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 36(1)(c) names three situations in which the procedure of the new enactment is followed and no others"

-- "as far as it can be adapted" is a limit in the words, so a procedure that cannot be adapted gets FALSE.
-- src:395 | 36 (1) If an enactment (the "former enactment") is repealed and another enactment (the "new enactment") is substituted for it,
-- src:398 | (c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed as far as it can be adapted in the recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment, in the enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment, and in a proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(c) (src:395, src:398)
GIVEN where IS A `Where the procedure of the new enactment is followed`
      `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the procedure established by the new enactment can be adapted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(c) the procedure established by the new enactment must be followed` where `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment` `the procedure established by the new enactment can be adapted` MEANS
    IF   `another enactment is substituted for the repealed enactment`
    THEN CONSIDER where
             WHEN `The recovery or enforcement of penalties and forfeitures incurred under the former enactment` THEN `the procedure established by the new enactment can be adapted`
             WHEN `The enforcement of rights existing or accruing under the former enactment` THEN `the procedure established by the new enactment can be adapted`
             WHEN `A proceeding relating to matters that happened before the repeal` THEN `the procedure established by the new enactment can be adapted`
             WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 36(1)(c) names three situations in which the procedure of the new enactment is followed and no others`
    ELSE `s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one`

§ `s 37 No implications from repeal, amendment, etc.`

DECLARE `What is done to an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `Repeal of all or part of it`
    `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it`
    `Amendment of it`
    `Consolidation of it`
    `Re-enactment of it`
    `Revision of it`

DECLARE `Something that might be read into what is done` IS ONE OF
    `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force`
    `A declaration about the previous state of the law`
    `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended`
    `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`
    `Something else`

-- src:405 | 37 (1) The repeal of all or part of an enactment, or the repeal of an enactment and the substitution for it of another enactment, or the amendment of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve either a declaration that the enactment was or was considered by the Legislature or other body or person who enacted it to have been previously in force, or a declaration about the previous state of the law.
-- src:406 | (2) The amendment of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve a declaration that the law under the enactment prior to the amendment was or was considered by the Legislature or other body or person who enacted it to have been different from the law under the enactment as amended.
-- src:407 | (3) An amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve an adoption of the construction that has by judicial decision or otherwise been placed on the language used in the enactment or on similar language.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 37 (src:405-407)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may"

-- Each cell of the grid of the three subsections is either named by the text ("must not be construed to be or to involve"),
-- which gives FALSE, or not named, which gives a refusal.
-- src:405 | 37 (1) The repeal of all or part of an enactment, or the repeal of an enactment and the substitution for it of another enactment, or the amendment of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve either a declaration that the enactment was or was considered by the Legislature or other body or person who enacted it to have been previously in force, or a declaration about the previous state of the law.
-- src:406 | (2) The amendment of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve a declaration that the law under the enactment prior to the amendment was or was considered by the Legislature or other body or person who enacted it to have been different from the law under the enactment as amended.
-- src:407 | (3) An amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision of an enactment must not be construed to be or to involve an adoption of the construction that has by judicial decision or otherwise been placed on the language used in the enactment or on similar language.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 37(1), (2) and (3) (src:405-407)
GIVEN done IS A `What is done to an enactment`
      read IS A `Something that might be read into what is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37 the thing may be read into what is done` done read MEANS
    CONSIDER read
        WHEN `A declaration that the enactment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, previously in force` THEN
            CONSIDER done
                WHEN `Repeal of all or part of it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Amendment of it` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may`
        WHEN `A declaration about the previous state of the law` THEN
            CONSIDER done
                WHEN `Repeal of all or part of it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Repeal of it and substitution of another enactment for it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Amendment of it` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may`
        WHEN `A declaration that the law under the enactment before the amendment was, or was considered by those who enacted it to have been, different from the law as amended` THEN
            CONSIDER done
                WHEN `Amendment of it` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may`
        WHEN `An adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN
            CONSIDER done
                WHEN `Amendment of it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Consolidation of it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Re-enactment of it` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Revision of it` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may`
        WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 37 says what must not be read into a repeal, amendment, consolidation, re-enactment or revision and does not say what may`
